/*
FLOW:

1. USER A SIGNS UP:
   - POST /api/users/signup
   - Request: { email: "userA@test.com", username: "userA", password: "pass123" }
   - Response: { id: "uuid-a", referral_code: "ABC12XY9", ... }
   - User A shares "ABC12XY9" with friends

2. USER B SIGNS UP (referred by User A):
   - POST /api/users/signup
   - Request: {
       email: "userB@test.com",
       username: "userB",
       password: "pass456",
       referred_by_code: "ABC12XY9"  // User B enters the code User A gave them
     }
   - Response: {
       id: "uuid-b",
       referral_code: "DEF45KL2",  // Auto-generated for User B
       referred_by_id: "uuid-a",   // Tracks that User B was referred by User A
       ...
     }

3. QUERY REFERRAL CHAIN:
   - Find all users referred by User A:
     SELECT * FROM user_login WHERE referred_by_id = 'uuid-a'
   
   - Find who referred User B:
     SELECT * FROM user_login WHERE id = 'uuid-a'  (from user_login.referred_by_id)

ADVANTAGES:
✓ No duplicate referral codes
✓ Unique code generated per user automatically
✓ Easy to track referral chains
✓ User just needs to share their referral_code
✓ Next user enters that code when signing up
✓ No conflicts or collisions
*/